        <mxCell id="erNote" value="The relationship the whole platform rests on:

one ORDER splits into one SHIPMENT per shop.

Three shops in one basket become three parcels, each collected from a different place, priced on its own distance and delivered separately. That is what makes this multi-vendor rather than one shop with several owners." style="shape=note;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;size=16;fillColor=#eef2ff;strokeColor=#4f46e5;align=left;spacingLeft=10;spacingTop=4;fontSize=11;verticalAlign=top;fontColor=#4338ca;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="1340" y="150" width="300" height="190" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="erNote2" value="Not shown: the legacy users and courier tables, which exist only so older databases keep working. See the schema diagram." style="shape=note;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;size=16;fillColor=#fffbeb;strokeColor=#b45309;align=left;spacingLeft=10;spacingTop=4;fontSize=11;verticalAlign=top;fontColor=#78350f;" vertex="1" parent="1">
